4. TELEMETRY AND NETWORK USE

The Software reads game telemetry on the computer where it runs. It can make a dashboard available to browsers on your local network. You control which browser requests to approve or remember, and can revoke remembered access in the app. Do not approve devices or users you do not trust. The app does not intentionally send your game telemetry to the Publisher.

The app stores remembered browser approvals and locally generated dashboard certificates on your computer. Browser connection details are used to handle access requests on your local network.

The readings are informational and depend on the game, telemetry plugin, computer, and network. They are not a substitute for the game's own displays and must not be used for vehicle control, safety-critical decisions, or emergency use. You are responsible for your network configuration and for keeping your devices and backups secure.

